          "code": "CSR_COMPLIANCE_ANALYSIS",
          "id": "1766153057617",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766153057618_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Context\nA social media compliance check ensures that the social media contents adhere to corporate social media policy, platform guidelines, and other internal guidelines. It involves monitoring the social media content and activities to identify and address potential risks and issues, helping protect your corporate reputation.\n\nInstruction\nGiven the social media post \"{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.webpost}}\", check if it has any of the following issues based on a general corporate social media policy.\nFor each issue, if a post appears to violate the policy respond with Yes, otherwise use No. Carefully follow these enhanced criteria:\n\nUses Profanity, the post does not use profanity.\nTreat any explicit or implied profane words as violations. Example words: \"idiots\", \"stupid\", \"clowns\", \"dumb\", and similar disrespectful language.\n\nIs Disparaging, the post does not disparage any companies, products, or people.\nFlag direct insults, sarcasm, jokes at the expense of others, or any content that criticizes individuals or organizations in a negative way.\n\nContains Confidential Information, the post does not appear to contain any information that might be considered confidential.\n\nA violation includes any mention of the words \"confidential\", \"internal use only\", \"not for public\", \"restricted\", \"proprietary\", \"private\", \"do not share externally\", \"sensitive\", \"classified\", or similar.\nAlso includes sharing: unreleased product/feature details, pricing, forecasts, HR or employee topics, legal/contracts, passwords or credentials, links or invites to internal resources, customer data, business strategies, or any other non-public corporate information.\nIf in doubt, treat as confidential and flag as a violation. \n\nDiscusses Future Offerings, the post does not discuss future offerings.\nAny reference to upcoming or unreleased products, features, partnerships, organizational changes, releases, versions, or events.\nFlag forward-looking phrases: \"coming soon,\" \"will be released,\" \"next month/quarter,\" \"stay tuned,\" \"watch for...\", or similar.\n\nMissing Disclaimer, ensure that the post contains a disclaimer that these are not the views of the organization, but rather the individual.\nThe disclaimer must be explicit. Acceptable wording includes: \"my views only\", \"personal opinion,\" \"not representing company,\" or similar.\nGeneric statements or implied meaning are insufficient.\n\nMissing References, if the post fails to provide proper context or attribution for the information or ideas presented.\nIf the post speculates on financials, mentions predictions, references “sources,” or presents unverified claims, it must include attribution, citation, or a disclaimer such as \"this is not investment advice.\"\nAny claim or statement requiring context or legality must have supporting reference or disclosure.\nAdditionally, for missing references:\n\nIf a post announces, predicts, speculates, or provides information about future events, features, performance, results, or releases, it must clearly state the source of the information (for example, \"according to the 2023 roadmap\" or \"per the official press release\") or include a compliance-friendly disclaimer such as \"not investment advice,\" \"results not guaranteed,\" or similar.\nForward-looking, impactful, or newsworthy claims must be backed by a reference to an approved, public source, or an appropriate legal/compliance disclaimer.\nAnnouncements, projections, or data without attribution or required disclosure should be flagged as missing references, even if the information may be widely known within the organization.\nFor every issue, return one and only one entry in the exact order above with \"Yes\" (if the post violates the policy) or \"No\" (if it is compliant). If unclear, err on the side of \"Yes.\"\n\nOutput Format\nOutput a valid RFC8259-compliant JSON object in the following format under a results key:\n{\n\"results\": [\n{\n\"issue\": \"\",\n\"result\": \"<insert Yes if the policy is violated, otherwise insert No>\"\n}\n]\n}\n\nAcceptance Criteria\nMake sure the JSON is valid without any extra words, commas, emojis, or backticks like ```json. \nReturn all results in the same order and with a single entry per issue."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
